{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingRecursion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBranchingRecursion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnumeration"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_branching_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_branching_5","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L219-L221","doc":"**(A) branching, `decide`-verified for `n = 5` (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_branching_le4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_branching_le4","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L213-L217","doc":"**(A) branching, `decide`-verified for `n ≤ 4` (sorry-free).** The Frame–Robinson–Thrall closed\nform satisfies the same recursion `dimHLF λ = Σ_{i corner} dimHLF(λ⁻ⁱ)`.  The decide-pinned target for\nthe eventual general `dimHLF_branching` (the pure β-number Lagrange identity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_branching_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_branching_5","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L209-L211","doc":"**(B) branching, `decide`-verified for `n = 5` (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_branching_le4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_branching_le4","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L203-L207","doc":"**(B) branching, `decide`-verified for `n ≤ 4` (sorry-free).** The brute-force `#SYT` satisfies the\ncorner-removal recursion `numSYTenum λ = Σ_{i corner} numSYTenum(λ⁻ⁱ)`.  The decide-pinned target for\nthe eventual general `numSYTenum_branching`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_dimHLF_of_branchings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_dimHLF_of_branchings","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L177-L201","doc":"**Composition: the hook-length formula from the two branching recursions (sorry-free).**\nGiven that both the brute-force count (B) and the closed form (A) satisfy the corner-removal\nrecursion on every positive-size sorted shape, `numSYTenum = dimHLF` for **all** sorted shapes — by\nstrong induction on `sz`, with `sz_decrementRow_lt` the termination measure and `sz = 0` the base.\nThis reduces the general-`n` hook-length formula (hence `dimAitkenIdentity`) to exactly (A) + (B). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_sz_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimHLF_sz_zero","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L173-L175","doc":"**Base dimension.** `dimHLF` of the empty shape is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.prodHooks_sz_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.prodHooks_sz_zero","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L157-L171","doc":"The hook product of the empty shape is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_sz_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_sz_zero","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L147-L155","doc":"**Base count.** The empty shape (`sz l = 0`) has exactly one standard tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.colsOK_replicate_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.colsOK_replicate_nil","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L138-L145","doc":"Columns of an all-empty layout are trivially strictly increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_nil","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L132-L136","doc":"`chunk l []` is all-empty rows: the empty filling laid out on shape `l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.decrementRow_sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.decrementRow_sorted","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L86-L123","doc":"**Corner removal preserves the partition shape.** Decrementing a removable corner keeps the row\nlengths weakly decreasing — the invariant the strong-induction hypotheses are stated over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sz_decrementRow_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sz_decrementRow_lt","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L76-L84","doc":"**The branching recursion is well-founded.** Every corner-removed shape is strictly smaller —\nthe termination measure (`sz`) for the strong induction that will compose (A)+(B) into the HLF. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_removableCornerIdxs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_removableCornerIdxs","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L70-L74","doc":"Membership in `removableCornerIdxs`: in range, and strictly longer than the row below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sz_decrementRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sz_decrementRow","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L57-L68","doc":"**Removing a cell drops the size by exactly one.** `sz (decrementRow l i) = sz l - 1` for any\nin-range positive row `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.getD_le_sz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.getD_le_sz","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L48-L55","doc":"Each row length is bounded by the total size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.branchSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.branchSum","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L38-L40","doc":"The branching sum `Σ_{i corner} F(λ⁻ⁱ)` for a count-valued `F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.removableCornerIdxs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.removableCornerIdxs","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L33-L36","doc":"The removable-corner row indices of `l`: rows strictly longer than the row below\n(`l.getD (i+1) 0 = 0` when there is no row below, so the last nonzero row always qualifies). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.decrementRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.decrementRow","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTBranchingRecursion.lean#L29-L31","doc":"Remove one cell from row `i`: decrement `l[i]` by `1` (a trailing `0` row is harmless — `chunk`\ngives it `0` cells, `prodHooks` an empty product, `sz` an unchanged sum). ","signatureChunk":0}]}